Your task is to convert natural language into a knowledge graph using valid Cypher queries.

You will be given a prompt in natural language, designated by <prompt>.
The prompt comes from a file, given after <file_path>.
The file is stored in a repository, given after <repo_path>.

Identify the entities and relationships in the prompt, the types of entities
and relationships, and the accompanying attributes.

CRITICAL CYPHER CONSTRAINTS:
- NEVER generate standalone MATCH statements (they are invalid)
- Use only CREATE and MERGE statements to build the knowledge graph
- Every statement must create or merge nodes and relationships
- Every NODE MUST have at least one LABEL. Choose from the taxonomy:
	Person, Organization, Company, Technology, Publication, Initiative, Facility, Application, Award.
	If none apply, use the fallback label Unknown (i.e., :Unknown).
- Do NOT create unlabeled nodes (labels(n) must never be empty)
- Always set 'file_path' and 'repo_path' attributes on all nodes and edges
- End each statement with a semicolon

VALID CYPHER EXAMPLES:
```cypher
CREATE (p:Person {{name: 'John Doe', file_path: '/path/to/file.md', repo_path: '/repo/path'}});
MERGE (c:Company {{name: 'Tech Corp', file_path: '/path/to/file.md', repo_path: '/repo/path'}});
CREATE (p)-[:WORKS_FOR {{since: '2020', file_path: '/path/to/file.md', repo_path: '/repo/path'}}]->(c);
// If type uncertain, use :Unknown to avoid unlabeled nodes
CREATE (x:Unknown {{name: 'Some Entity', file_path: '/path/to/file.md', repo_path: '/repo/path'}});
```

INVALID CYPHER (DO NOT GENERATE):
```cypher
MATCH (p:Person {{name: 'John Doe'}});  // INVALID - standalone MATCH
MATCH (c:Company) RETURN c.name;      // INVALID - use CREATE/MERGE instead
CREATE (n {name: 'No Label'});         // INVALID - unlabeled node
```

Convert the prompt into valid Cypher CREATE and MERGE statements only.
Pay special attention to relationship directions and ensure all entities have proper attributes.
Set the attribute 'file_path' of every node and edge created equal to the source of the prompt.
Set the attribute 'repo_path' of every node and edge created equal to the repository where the prompt comes from.